      <h1>Gutter Installation in the Shoals, AL</h1>
      <p class="location-intro">Most gutter estimates in the Shoals are quoting the wrong part of the job. The aluminum is the cheap, easy piece — the part that decides whether the work lasts is the wood it hangs on. Across the region's older housing, gutters bolt onto fascia board and rafter tails that have been catching overflow for fifty and sixty years, and on a lot of homes that board is soft. So a Shoals gutter job is less about the trough and more about the carpentry behind it — which is why the same install is a straight swap on a new Muscle Shoals house and a genuine repair project on an old one in Sheffield or Florence.</p>
